    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\nD0D9854FCA16AFE445E8527903B3C142A848AA8762A01FA7E97B8C7EC494084E3AE65E635796\n\n### Feature Description\n\nCurrently, when receiving a new message in qTox, a closed envelope icon appears next to the contact, indicating there are unread messages. Once the chat window is opened, the message is marked as read and the envelope disappears.\n\nHowever, there is no way to manually mark a conversation as unread after reading. This can be inconvenient when a user wants to come back to a message later or needs a reminder to follow up.\n\nSuggested feature:\n\n    Add an option (right-click on contact, or via chat menu) to mark conversation as unread.\n\n    When applied, the envelope icon (or a similar visual notification) should reappear, indicating there are messages pending attention.\n\n    Optionally, add a visible indicator in the contact list or conversation view.\n\nBenefits:\n✅ Helps users keep track of conversations they need to revisit.\n✅ Improves usability for users managing multiple contacts or busy message flows.\n✅ Aligns qTox with other modern messaging apps (e.g., Telegram, WhatsApp, email clients) that support “Mark as Unread”.\n\nPossible implementation notes:\n\n    This feature can affect only the local client state (no need for network synchronization).\n\n    It could be stored in the local config or cache, similar to how unread status is currently managed.\n\nThank you for your work maintaining and improving qTox!\n\n### Contribution\n\n- [ ] I would like to contribute to this feature",
